---
description: Baron Aerial Media shared safety and development workflow
alwaysApply: true
---
- Work in a feature branch and open a draft PR; never merge or deploy to Hetzner automatically.
- Do not read, echo, commit, or copy live .env files, private keys, tokens, production database contents, or client media into prompts/logs.
- Treat production and NAS development as separate security boundaries. Use synthetic fixture data.
- Edit only the current repository unless explicitly tasked with coordinated changes.
- Before PR: run relevant typecheck, tests, lint, build/Compose checks; report failures clearly rather than claiming success.
- Migrations must be reviewed and applied separately; never run automatically in a Docker build or PR.
- Entra ID: prefer OIDC; never assume GROK_AUTH_* is compatible with native Microsoft Entra.
- AIR integration: consume only approved, versioned media export manifests, never unreviewed source media.
- Prefer smallest changes, preserve reviewed photography provenance and avoid fabricated business/FAA claims.
